{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvQmxhY2slMjBOYXJjaXNzdXMlMjAlMjgxOTQ3JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Black Narcissus","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/jSbFWWbkUq5N5ikewJHNATcWnxS.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/hAyWibhJjMHyWXrMVX8N2MrEqF8.jpg","description":"A group of Anglican nuns, led by Sister Clodagh, are sent to a mountain in the Himalayas. The climate in the region is hostile and the nuns are housed in an odd old palace. They work to establish a school and a hospital, but slowly their focus shifts. Sister Ruth falls for a government worker, Mr. Dean, and begins to question her vow of celibacy. As Sister Ruth obsesses over Mr. Dean, Sister Clodagh becomes immersed in her own memories of love.","releaseInfo":"1947","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.5","runtime":"100 min","cast":["Deborah Kerr","Sabu","David Farrar","Flora Robson","Esmond Knight","Jean Simmons","Kathleen Byron","Jenny Laird"],"director":["Emeric Pressburger","Michael Powell"],"released":"1947-05-26T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"A story of exquisite yearning in a strange and beautiful land. Towering over the screen ... as the mountains that saw it happen.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Deborah Kerr","character":"Sister Clodagh","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/dHFhOEhHnn5cQjQN29IGRxzoxBP.jpg"},{"name":"Sabu","character":"The Young General","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4tBtK9Hi4Plns5AP7sjixaWJZat.jpg"},{"name":"David Farrar","character":"Mr. Dean","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/d4CJBDYWhNnYXqEFmXi0dG2cPJK.jpg"},{"name":"Flora Robson","character":"Sister Philippa","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/8Ptdv8auJVrXEzx0lzkzpcaXNu8.jpg"},{"name":"Esmond Knight","character":"The Old General","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ka4eJaGtMlghVQnVcQOFSFEb2uA.jpg"},{"name":"Jean Simmons","character":"Kanchi","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/scbR91Bl4SbfQqhXaH6Ofh